{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463202",
      "title": "Methods vs Computed Properties vs Watchers",
      "lectureOrder": 33,
      "videoOrder": 29,
      "sourceHash": "0a67f20a767d3f5dcceda9340989d2b3eaa6f9765571ad3e0908172e42848e5b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.532,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "I know that there's,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "Methods vs Computed vs Watchers thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 8,
          "en": "Can be very confusing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8,
          "end": 10.24,
          "en": "So it's time for a short summary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.24,
          "end": 15.07,
          "en": "Methods can be used in your template to bind data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.07,
          "end": 17.8,
          "en": "to use them in a interpolation, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.8,
          "end": 20.4,
          "en": "To derive data that should be used in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 22.12,
          "en": "or for event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.12,
          "end": 24.29,
          "en": "You can use methods for both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.29,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "And if you use them in the data binding use case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "so if you use them between curly braces, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 33.72,
          "en": "to outsource logic from the template to your view instance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 35.36,
          "en": "then the method is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.36,
          "end": 38.5,
          "en": "for every re-render cycle of the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.5,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "So whenever something changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 42.02,
          "en": "and the template is re-evaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.02,
          "end": 44.17,
          "en": "every method that's called in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.17,
          "end": 45.4,
          "en": "will be called again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.4,
          "end": 47.8,
          "en": "That's what I showed you a couple of lectures ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.8,
          "end": 48.91,
          "en": "And therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 48.91,
          "end": 53.01,
          "en": "you should use methods primarily for event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 54.62,
          "en": "There it's a no brainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.62,
          "end": 55.97,
          "en": "You always use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.97,
          "end": 58.2,
          "en": "or for data binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.2,
          "end": 60.84,
          "en": "so with double curly braces, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 60.84,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "if you really want them to re-execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 65.961,
          "en": "whenever something changes on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 65.961,
          "end": 68.06,
          "en": "Otherwise, you use computed properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 68.06,
          "end": 70.47,
          "en": "because those can only be used with data binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 70.47,
          "end": 72.7,
          "en": "You don't use them with event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 72.7,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "And computed properties are great to derive data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "that's based on other data with the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 84.78999999999999,
          "en": "that they will only be re-evaluated and re-executed by view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 84.78999999999999,
          "end": 87.14,
          "en": "if the dependent data changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.14,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "So if the data used inside of the computed property changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "they will not be re-evaluated if some other data changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 99.35,
          "en": "And therefore, use them for data that depends on other data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.86,
          "end": 100.92,
          "en": "Last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 104.06,
          "en": "Watchers are not directly used in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.06,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "You don't reference them there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 108.14,
          "en": "but you can watch any property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 108.14,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "even computed properties with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 112.63,
          "en": "And that allows you to run code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 112.63,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "in reaction to some change data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 117.05,
          "en": "For example, to send the HTTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 117.05,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "set a timer, stores something in local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 121.07,
          "en": "whatever it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 121.07,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "So typically, you should use Watchers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 126.55,
          "en": "for any non data updates you wanna make.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 126.55,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "Whatever you got some behind the scenes work to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 131.04,
          "en": "based on some changing data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 131.04,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "you might wanna consider a Watcher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 135.08,
          "en": "Amongst the free Watchers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 135.08,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "are probably the feature you'll use the least",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 140.86,
          "en": "because you need methods all the time with event binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 140.86,
          "end": 143.54,
          "en": "and computed properties for outputting data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 143.54,
          "end": 144.953,
          "en": "that depends on other data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
